We have, $f(x)=\log (1-x)+\sqrt{x^{2}-1}\log (1-x)$ is defined if $1-x > 0 \Rightarrow x < 1\Rightarrow \quad x \in(-\infty,-1) \quad \text{...(i)} 
and $\sqrt{x^{2}-1} is defined if $ x^{2}-1 \geq 0 \begin{array}{ll}
\Rightarrow& x^{2} \geq 1 \\
\Rightarrow & x \geq 1 \text{ or } x \leq-1 \quad \text{...(ii)}
\end{array}$ By Eqs. (i) and (ii), required domain is $(-\infty,-1]$.
